  "details": "In VRChat’s Camera Dolly feature, when I add a second path (or more), the recording view from the second camera displays a green border. I am unable to control zoom or set keyframes for this camera. Also, when I click the camera settings to adjust lens visibility, it only affects the first path’s camera; the second and subsequent cameras remain uncontrolled and their visibility cannot be changed.\n\nOpen Camera Dolly (VRC+).\n\nCreate a first path and set up a camera.\n\nAdd a second (or third) path.\n\nObserve the green border on the second camera’s preview.\n\nTry to adjust zoom or set a keyframe – nothing happens.\n\nTry to change lens visibility – only the first camera responds.\n\nExpected behavior: All paths’ cameras should allow zoom keyframing and visibility control independently.\n\nActual behavior: Only the first path works; additional paths are visually marked with a green border and are unresponsive to zoom and visibility controls.",
